    "vulnerability_2_the_high_dose_sedation_trap": "Camp A's point that fibromyalgia pain requires 1,800–2,400 mg/day of gabapentin monotherapy—which produces catastrophic daytime somnolence and cognitive slowing in a patient already complaining of 'extremely fatigue' and 'diminished cognitive ability'—has no clinical counter. Gabapentin low-dose (300–600 mg) only works for fibromyalgia when potentiated by Duloxetine!",
